{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461463-v20-importing-my-favorite-aspects-of-v5-to-v20","id":1461463,"title":"[V20] Importing My Favorite Aspects of V5 to V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-25T19:24:43-07:00","id":1461463,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Importing My Favorite Aspects of V5 to V20","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\">I started with V5, and I did, and still kind of do, enjoy it. However, I have since played V20, and it has become my favorite system. That said, there are some things that V5 did that I actually like, so I stole them and repurposed them for V20. I also added some things that I don't like as much, but decided to give people more options.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Antitribu</span><br /> In the past, the term Antitribu was used to describe division within a clan in which opposed the main body of the clan. The resulting bloodline would have been labeled &lt;Clan Name&gt; Antitribu. However, in V5 the term has undergone a change that I actually approve of. The term now means \u201canti-clans\u201d, and is used to describe the Sabbat\u2019s distaste towards the idea of acknowledging clan or lineage<sup>1</sup>. I really prefer this change, so here\u2019s how to add it to V20.</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Change: </b></i>The word Antitribu is added after the clan, or bloodline, on the character sheet to show the character shares the Sabbat view of clans, even Lasombra and Tzimisce. Mechanically, there is no difference between an Antitribu and a normal member of the clan or bloodline. Roleplay wise, any Antitribu will rarely hide their derision for clans, lineage, or similar concepts in social situations<sup>1</sup>.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Hecata</span><br /> I actually don\u2019t hate the Hecata as a concept, but I agree that it was weirdly implemented. Adding them to a V20 is actually pretty easy though, and here 3 options on how to do it.</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Option 1: </b></i>Just Make them a Sect. It is that simple. Read Cults of the Blood Gods to learn how the sect could operate.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Option 2: </b></i>Make them a new Clan. This is also pretty easy to do, but honestly, Option 1 is even easier. To make them a clan, simply give them Auspex, Fortitude, and Necromancy as in-clan disciplines. Also give them the Giovanni weakness. After that, you\u2019re done.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Option 3: </b></i>Just replace the weakness of the Hecata Bloodlines. So I like this option the least, but here\u2019s how to do it. Basically, take the Cappadocians, Harbingers of Skull, Samedi, and Nagaraja bloodlines and replace their clan weakness with the Giovanni clan weakness.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Tzimisce Bane</span><br /> The best thing in V5, in my opinion, was the change to the Tzimisce\u2019s clan weakness. So I literally just took that weakness and gave it the old weakness\u2019s penalty. If you\u2019re to lazy to do this yourself, don\u2019t worry I got you:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each Tzimisce must choose a specific charge \u2014 a physical domain, a group of people, an organization, or even something more esoteric \u2014 but clearly defined and limited. The Kindred must spend their daysleep, surrounded by their chosen charge. Historically, this has often meant slumbering in the soil of their land, but it can also mean being surrounded by that which they tonight rule: a certain kind of people, a building deeply tied to their obsession, a local counterculture faction, or other, more outlandish elements. For each day of rest not surrounded by their charge, halve all dice pools (round down), cumulatively, until the pool reaches one die. A full day of proper rest with their chosen charge will restore the dice pools to their normal value.<sup>2</sup> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Tremere Bane</span><br /> Due to in game events, the Tremere blood has actually lost the ability to bond. If you want to simulate this change, here\u2019s a rewrite of the bane from V5 for your V20 game:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere vitae can no longer Blood Bond other Kindred, though they themselves can be bound by Kindred from other clans. A Tremere can still bind mortals and ghouls, though it requires two additional draughts of blood for the bond to form.<sup>3</sup> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Assimite Changes</span><br /> Call them Banu Haqim, and use the weakness on page 428 of the core book<sup>4</sup>. Also pretend the skin growing darker with age was never mentioned. That is all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Ravnos Bane</span><br /> I\u2019ll be frank, I didn\u2019t want to rewrite the Ravnos or Tremere V5 banes for V20. However, I did it because I did Tzimisce, and felt obligated to do it. Here I go, I guess.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Ravnos slumbers in the same place more than once in seven nights, they roll their Courage (Difficulty 5+each day they slumbered in the same place). They receive aggravated damage equal to the number of successes as they are scorched from within. This happens every time they spend the day in a location they\u2019ve already slumbered less than a week before. What constitutes a location in this regard depends on the scope of the chronicle, but unless otherwise stated, two resting places need to be at least a mile apart to avoid triggering the Bane. Furthermore, a mobile haven, such as a movers\u2019 truck, is safe so long as the place where the truck is parked is at least a mile from the last location. Ravnos characters cannot take the Domain Background at character creation.<sup>5</sup> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Salubri Bane</span><br /> Haven't they suffered enough? The answer is yes!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup> See page 74 of Sabbat: The Black Hand for more details.<br /> <sup>2</sup> See pages 18-19 of 5th Edition Companion for the original bane. It's basically the same though.<br /> <sup>3</sup> See page 97 of Vampire The Masquerade 5th Edition for the original bane. Still basically the same.<br /> <sup>4 </sup>See page 428 of Vampire The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <sup>5 </sup>See page 9 of 5th Edition Companion for the original bane.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T00:01:19-07:00","id":1461490,"title":"","content":"You got yourself the seal <b>Approved by an Old-Timer</b>. I play since 1st edition and liked every single one of your changes. At most I would think about letting a Salubri player chose between the two weaknesses, but that's it.<br /> <br /> The Tremere lack of Blood Bond is extremely fitting for their history, since they're arguably not real Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:27:33-07:00","id":1461509,"title":"","content":"The only thing that I'd be concerned about is the Tremere change depending on how much you decide to change the Tremere from their pre-V5 culture (which is highly dependent on blood bonds) to their V5 status.<br /> <br /> There's also somethings to consider regarding how learning Disciplines works. One of the ways that the Tremere keep Thaumaturgy to themselves (even with the Revised era's explosion of alternatives) is that non-Tremere trying to learn Thaumaturgy had to drink Tremere blood and thus risk getting bound to them; something most vampires are extremely hesitant to do esp. with the Clan's internal unity generally being bad for any outsider that manages to get a tutor in the first place. So there's some social implications present in this that's more relevant in V20 than it is in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://for