re (which is highly dependent on blood bonds) to their V5 status.<br /> <br /> There's also somethings to consider regarding how learning Disciplines works. One of the ways that the Tremere keep Thaumaturgy to themselves (even with the Revised era's explosion of alternatives) is that non-Tremere trying to learn Thaumaturgy had to drink Tremere blood and thus risk getting bound to them; something most vampires are extremely hesitant to do esp. with the Clan's internal unity generally being bad for any outsider that manages to get a tutor in the first place. So there's some social implications present in this that's more relevant in V20 than it is in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>These options are to help play a v20 game using more v5 lore, in which most Tremere don't reveal this development to the wider public. Considering it's easier to import to v20 from v5 instead of the vice versa, that's what I did. However, I personally don't change Tremere or Ravnos weaknesses unless I want to go all in on v5 changes. That said, those new weaknesses have an in lore reason behind them, unlike the Salubri's. Still can't find a good lore reason why their weaknesses changed in v5, so I said I did enough and left it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Typos 09-26-2021, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T10:38:11-07:00","id":1461569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461463-v20-importing-my-favorite-aspects-of-v5-to-v20?p=1461555#post1461555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So option 1 essentially.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sect requires a proactive pan clan agenda and excludes membership from other sects so no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T12:24:48-07:00","id":1461587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461463-v20-importing-my-favorite-aspects-of-v5-to-v20?p=1461569#post1461569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A sect requires a proactive pan clan agenda and excludes membership from other sects so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different interpretations of what a sect is, I think. But on a strict interpretation using the two canon groups using the word, yeah, you're right.<br /> <br /> The new Tremere weakness makes sense for them. They're not strictly Cainites, so it would make far more sense for their method of becoming to have a flaw once compared to &quot;true vampirism&quot; makes sense instead of the perfection of being curseless vampires. Even the Nagaraja, that used a version of frigging Spell of Life with they could base on the real deal, had a weakness raised from their Paradigm and aren't real vampires (they use the same rules, but they don't really need the blood. Their anthropophagy is in-lore more akin to a Paradox effect on what would otherwise be a curseless vampire).<br /> <br /> Ravnos' previous weaknesses are either dumb (1st ed), profoundly racist (2nd ed to V20) or disguising racism by becoming Compulsion to do What I Would Anyway (DA V20 and the lightning strikes twice). The new weakness is at least less evil racism, justify the clan wandering without the need for saying <i>&quot;they do 'cause gypsies&quot;</i>, and makes for interesting dynamics in the game without making the PC a mandated asshole within the group.<br /> <br /> As much as I like the Healer Salubri and used their weakness gladly, the new one is cool and justifies far more other vampires having hunted them instead of not heeding the advice of known cheaters and diablerists to strike down the guys that could heal Aggravated for 2 Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T05:30:42-07:00","id":1461668,"title":"","content":"One of the main changes I implemented was a variation on V5\u2019s take on Generation. Not the blood potency part, but the idea that instead of costing background points the PC generations (8-16) all had various tradeoffs.<br /> <br /> The big one was adding a Bane Strength based on generation and adjusted clan weaknesses accordingly (ex. Brujah have their difficulty to resist frenzy increased by Bane Strength).<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s the chart;<br /> <br /> 8th: BP 15/3; Bane 3, +1 diff to degeneration checks.<br /> 9th: BP 14/2; Bane 3<br /> 10th: BP 13/1; Bane 2<br /> 11th: BP 12/1; Bane 2; full nourishment from cold blood<br /> 12th: BP 11/1; Bane 1; cold blood<br /> 13th: BP 10/1; Bane 1; cold blood, eat food merit<br /> 14th: BP 8/1; Bane 0; cold blood, eat food, soak sun w. stamina (aggravated)<br /> 15th: BP 6/1; Bane 0; cold blood, eat food, soak sun (lethal)<br /> 16th: BP 4/1; Bane 0; cold blood, eat food, soak sun (bashing)<br /> <br /> 7th and lower generations start breaking the balance curve (increased trait caps, much higher blood pools with the trade off being mostly slightly higher bane strength; 4 for 6-7th, 5 for 5-4th; and increased difficulty for degeneration checks; +1 for 7th, +2 for 5-6th, +3 for 4th) so there\u2019s still a point to diablerie, it\u2019s just more a tradeoff from 16th to 8th before you start getting the real rewards (and, by the time you\u2019re a veritable blood god, who cares about trivialities like morality?).<br /> <br /> In reworking the weaknesses so they\u2019d have something Bane related I also took some inspiration from V5\u2019s banes; ex. Ventrue can spend Bane willpower points to feed from someone other than their chosen prey type.<br /> <br /> I really didn\u2019t like the V5 Ravnos bane; it\u2019s way too severe relative to the others and makes them much harder to integrate into a normal PC group. So instead they lose Bane willpower on waking if they failed to indulge their vice during the prior night. I also loosened up what counts as a vice a bit\u2026 one in my campaign is a shopaholic and must buy things they don\u2019t need and another is addicted to their tech blogs and must catch up on them every night. Basically, if it eats up part of your life that could be better spent it\u2019s a vice.<br /> <br /> I also prefer the Tzimisce flaw of having a \u201ccharge\u201d that might be territory but might also be a people. It adds more flexibility to the concept.<br /> <br /> I also tweaked a few discipline powers. Ex. I like V5\u2019s take on Presence 1 as adding dice to your normal social tests\u2026 basically like V20 Potence and Celerity. Particularly since the effects of default Presence 1 use the same dice pool and difficulty as a mundane Performance check which has similar resul In terms of affecting attitudes.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, mostly I fiddled on the mechanics side. My latest campaign just had news of the attack on Vienna hit about two weeks ago game time and no one knows what happened and the local regent/Primogen for city has gone missing in the aftermath and he\u2019d divided the duties of deputy regent and clan whip to two different underlings who are now vying for power as acting regent and acting Primogen respectively (the one point both agree on was the Regent/Primogen had left for Vienna for an important meeting a week before the attack and so he is presumed dead; no one\u2019s bothered to investigate the disappearance, but there are still clues that could be followed to see if that is really the case\u2026 if anyone cared enough to bother).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:20:19-07:00","id":1461700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461463-v20-importing-my-favorite-aspects-of-v5-to-v20?p=1461587#post1461587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravnos' previous weaknesses are either dumb (1st ed), profoundly racist (2nd ed to V20) or disguising racism by becoming Compulsion to do What I Would Anyway (DA V20 and the lightning strikes twice). The new weakness is at least less evil racism, justify the clan wandering without the need for saying <i>&amp;quot;they do 'cause gypsies&amp;quot;</i>, and makes for interesting dynamics in the game without making the PC a mandated asshole within the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I won't deny the weaknesses for most of VTM history was racist in context with their lore, it doesn't mandate the player has to pick a vice like stealing or murder. In fact it can honestly anything culturally seen as immoral, which can include things like hoarding and vanity. In the case of the former, the vampire becomes unable to part with almost anything they've received. For vanity, a vampire will effectively become a toreador around reflective surfaces.<br /> <br /> I actually prefer the DA20 version, mostly because of the inclusion of virtues. In fact I actually came up with an Ancille Ravnos NPC with the Virtue of charity. They effectively spend all their time tending to the down trotten and needy souls. The best part, they hate this! They've spent 100+ years forced into a situation they can't bring themselves to escape. The little they can force themselves away from his work is to go hunting. This is quickly ended soon after as the need to give all his time to others slowly drives him insane. It's an awful situation, based on a twisted idea of charity.<br /> <br /> That all said, most PCs will just pick an asshole vice sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:19:51-07:00","id":1461724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461463-v20-importing-my-favorite-aspects-of-v5-to-v20?p=1461668#post1461668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really didn\u2019t like the V5 Ravnos bane; it\u2019s way too severe relative to the others and makes them much harder to integrate into a normal PC group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think the new Ravnos Bane so disruptive. To me, setting up 8+ havens across the city isn't exceptionally hard or disruptive, unless you really want all the PCs living together, which isn't the game's premise. The Ravnos can meet them at the same place every night if they want without any problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:08:10-07:00","id":1461741,"title":"","content":"That's very dependent on the setup of a given city. Maintaining a bunch of zero dot Havens is easy enough in theory, but gets a lot harder when you have to take feeding and domain into account.<br /> <br /> If you're an ST that designs things after the players make their characters, it's unlikely to be too bad. If you're a sandbox ST that makes up a whole setting to let the players loose in, it can be really punishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:42:45-07:00","id":1461749,"title":"","content":"But feeding isn't covered by the weakness, and transportation ins't likely to be a big concern. Domain may or may not be a problem, but I see that more as an opportunity for stories than anything, as the character must decide how to maneuver the domains of the city. As long as they don't feed in a given domain, though, I tend to consider that even without authorization the character will hardly be even found, and if found thing aren't likely to immediately escalate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:19:35-07:00","id":1461756,"title":"","content":"Feeding isn't covered by the weakness, but it is impacted by the weakness. How do you maintain a Herd if you're constantly moving around the city? If you're avoid feeding in domains, it means the best feeding spots are off-limits, and you're feeding is going to be harder and/or more time consuming (on top of all the time you're spending with excess moving around the city, and needing to make sure your haven is in functional condition after leaving it alone for a few nights).<br /> <br /> Again, style and setup is going to matter, a lot, to how this plays. But to an extent that's kinda the problem. It's a weakness that could be crippling or nothing depending on some very common gaming approaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}